note check: the gate. The gate needs one pass or fail answer, so a hook can refuse a commit while the map is stale (design.md section 5). Prints the same listing as stale and then 'ok' when nothing is stale and no link is broken; otherwise ends with an error naming the counts and the process exits 2. No arguments. The CLAUDE.md contract requires it to pass before a commit, and the exit code is what makes it usable from a hook. A map with a merge conflict in it never gets this far: the load itself refuses it.

